  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Our dreams come from a part of the brain that contains our thoughts and memories."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "A person can have up to six dreams a night."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Each one usually lasts from 10 to 40 minutes."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Everyone dreams, but not everyone remembers their dreams."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Most people dream in color, usually with sound."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "And we usually dream about ourselves and the people we know."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "Why Do We Dream?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Alan Siegel is a scientist who studies dreams."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "“[Dreams] can tell us a lot about ourselves,” he says, “and can help us figure out problems.”"
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Another scientist, Robert Stickgold, thinks dreams come from our memories."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Stickgold says that dreaming about past events is useful because it helps us learn from them."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Here are a few types of dreams and what people think they mean."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "This dream may be the result of an embarrassing 1 event in your life."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "Some people think we dream about embarrassing situations if our brains are trying to deal with 2 an event in our own lives."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "If you dream about flying, you are probably quite happy."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "This is a good period in your life."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "You may feel that other people see you as a leader."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "This probably means you are worried about an important future event."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "If you haven’t prepared for it, your dream may be telling you, “It’s time to get to work!”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
